{
  "_comment": [
    "The load order, defined once.",
    "",
    "Every drift bug Peek has had came from this list existing in three places:",
    "Firefox's manifest, Chrome's manifest, and Chrome's offscreen.html. A module",
    "added to one and forgotten in another fails only in the browser that missed",
    "it, and only at runtime \u2014 'P.policy.forHost is not a function' on every link.",
    "",
    "build.py generates all three from this file. Add a module here and it lands",
    "everywhere it belongs, or nowhere.",
    "",
    "Paths are relative to src/, except vendor/, which is copied as-is.",
    "Order matters: these are classic scripts sharing a Peek namespace, so a",
    "module must come after anything it reads at load time."
  ],
  "content": [
    "common/log.js",
    "config/rules.js",
    "config/sites.js",
    "config/trackers.js",
    "platform/dom.js",
    "common/text.js",
    "common/url.js",
    "common/policy.js",
    "link/tld.js",
    "link/recognizers.js",
    "link/nav.js",
    "link/analyze.js",
    "content/styles.js",
    "content/settings.js",
    "content/build.js",
    "content/card.js",
    "content/hover.js",
    "content/index.js"
  ],
